{
  "_comment": "Conformance cases for parse_plan, the proxy reading a capture plan Rail Center serves to the agent below. `plan` is the capture design's worked example (its section 2), its body paths under request; each case is that plan with `patch` applied (RFC 6902: add, remove, replace), or `bytes` as sent. `expect` is `refused` (`not_json`, `no_content_hash`, `other_agent`), or a `reading`: `valid`, with the first entry's conditions as read (`valid`, `unknown`, `invalid`) where given; `unknown`; `redaction_mismatch`; or `invalid`, `at` the field its reason starts with. `plan_version`, where given, is as read, null where it doesn't read. The proxy's ceilings: window_seconds 60 to 86400, max_groups_per_window up to 100000, max_steps_per_window up to 1000000, max_unsent_windows up to 1000.",
  "agent": {
    "host_id": "host-7f3c",
    "sandbox_name": "agent-finretail"
  },
  "plan": {
    "schema_version": "1.0",
    "content_hash": "sha256:fb3733bbe47258024770ac2cc2521f60c5709ddc2a31b87744ed1c213229d77c",
    "generated_at": "2026-11-10T09:58:02Z",
    "agent": {
      "host_id": "host-7f3c",
      "sandbox_name": "agent-finretail"
    },
    "plan_version": 7,
    "redaction_version": 1,
    "window_seconds": 900,
    "budget": {
      "max_groups_per_window": 1000,
      "max_steps_per_window": 10000,
      "on_max_groups": "coarsen_to_catch_all",
      "max_unsent_windows": 8
    },
    "entries": [
      {
        "id": "e1",
        "match": [
